#
# ✒ Changelog:
#     - 2.2.0 (11/09/2026) [dendogg + Anthropic - Claude Opus 5.5] — Created
#       on Dennis's direction to harden the GitHub Pages build.
#
# ✒ Description:
#     Tells GitHub Pages to publish the repository as-is instead of running
#     it through Jekyll. GitHub checks only that this file exists; its
#     contents are never read, so this header is safe.
#
# ✒ Key Features:
#     - Files are served byte for byte, as the no-build-step stack expects.
#     - No Liquid pass over the Markdown and no Jekyll exclusion rules, so
#       nothing can be silently dropped or rewritten.
#     - Faster branch deploys: there is no site generator to run.
#
# ✒ Other Important Information:
#     - Dependencies: none
#     - Compatible platforms: GitHub Pages "Deploy from a branch"; ignored
#       by the GitHub Actions deploy in .github/workflows/pages.yml, which
#       never runs Jekyll
# ---------
